§ `Part 5A - Release of security bond`

§§ `Division 1 - Application for release`

§§§ `81C. Application for release of security bond`

DECLARE `security bond release application` HAS
    `the applicant is one, some or all of the parties to the residential tenancy agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the application is in the approved form` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the application states the amount of the security bond to be paid to each party` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the residential tenancy agreement has terminated` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the tenant or all cotenants have delivered up vacant possession of the premises` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the parties to the agreement have agreed in writing to terminate the agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
    `section 81D applies` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN a IS A `security bond release application`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 81C(4) applies` IF
        a's `the tenant or all cotenants have delivered up vacant possession of the premises`
    AND a's `the parties to the agreement have agreed in writing to terminate the agreement`

@ref Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) s.81C
@export Decide whether a security bond release application may be made under s.81C
GIVEN a IS A `security bond release application` @desc One, some or all parties may apply to the bond administrator in the approved form stating amounts to be paid to each party. Must not be made before the agreement terminates, unless the tenants have delivered up vacant possession and the parties have agreed in writing to terminate, or s.81D (partial release) applies.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a security bond release application may be made` IF
        a's `the applicant is one, some or all of the parties to the residential tenancy agreement`
    AND a's `the application is in the approved form`
    AND a's `the application states the amount of the security bond to be paid to each party`
    AND (
            a's `the residential tenancy agreement has terminated`
        OR  `section 81C(4) applies` a
        OR  a's `section 81D applies`
        )

§§§ `81D. Application for partial release of security bond`

DECLARE `partial bond release application` HAS
    `the application is under section 81C` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the application is for only part of a security bond to be released` IS A BOOLEAN
    `that part is to be paid to the tenant or 1 or more of the cotenants` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the rent payable under the residential tenancy agreement has been reduced` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the tenant paid the prescribed pet bond amount and the pet is no longer being kept on the premises` IS A BOOLEAN
    `other prescribed circumstances exist` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) s.81D
@export Decide whether a partial security bond release application may be made under s.81D
GIVEN a IS A `partial bond release application` @desc An s.81C application for only part of the bond, payable to the tenant or one or more cotenants. Allowed only if rent has been reduced, the prescribed pet bond was paid and the pet is no longer kept, or other prescribed circumstances exist. s.81C(3) does not apply to a partial application.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a partial security bond release application may be made` IF
        a's `the application is under section 81C`
    AND a's `the application is for only part of a security bond to be released`
    AND a's `that part is to be paid to the tenant or 1 or more of the cotenants`
    AND (
            a's `the rent payable under the residential tenancy agreement has been reduced`
        OR  a's `the tenant paid the prescribed pet bond amount and the pet is no longer being kept on the premises`
        OR  a's `other prescribed circumstances exist`
        )

§§§ `81E. Amounts for which lessor is entitled to payment from security bond`

DECLARE `bond claim` HAS
    `the amount is the reasonable cost of repairs to the premises, or restoration to original condition, as a result of damage other than fair wear and tear caused by the tenant, an occupant or an invitee of the tenant` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the amount is the reasonable cost of repairs to or replacement of chattels provided with the premises as a result of damage other than fair wear and tear caused by the tenant, an occupant or an invitee of the tenant` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the amount is rent or other charges owing and payable under the agreement or this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the amount is the cost of cleaning any part of the premises not left reasonably clean by the tenant having regard to the condition of the premises at the start of the tenancy` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the amount is the cost of replacing locks or other security devices altered, removed or added by the tenant without the consent of the lessor` IS A BOOLEAN
    `section 50ZD(2) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the amount is an amount the tenant is liable to pay to the lessor for a breach of the agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the amount is prescribed as an amount for which the lessor is not entitled to payment from the security bond` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the security bond includes the prescribed pet bond amount` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the amount is the reasonable cost of repairs or restoration as a result of damage caused by a pet kept at the premises` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the amount is the reasonable cost of fumigating the premises because a pet kept on the premises is capable of carrying parasites that can affect humans` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the amount is other reasonable costs arising out of the keeping of the pet on the premises` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) s.81E
@export Decide whether the lessor is entitled to payment of a claimed amount from the security bond under s.81E
GIVEN c IS A `bond claim` @desc Set the matching s.81E(1) limb, or a pet-bond limb under s.81E(2) if the bond includes the prescribed pet amount. The lessor is not entitled to a prescribed excluded amount. Lock-replacement is subject to s.50ZD(2).
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the lessor is entitled to payment of the amount from the security bond` IF
        NOT c's `the amount is prescribed as an amount for which the lessor is not entitled to payment from the security bond`
    AND (
            c's `the amount is the reasonable cost of repairs to the premises, or restoration to original condition, as a result of damage other than fair wear and tear caused by the tenant, an occupant or an invitee of the tenant`
        OR  c's `the amount is the reasonable cost of repairs to or replacement of chattels provided with the premises as a result of damage other than fair wear and tear caused by the tenant, an occupant or an invitee of the tenant`
        OR  c's `the amount is rent or other charges owing and payable under the agreement or this Act`
        OR  c's `the amount is the cost of cleaning any part of the premises not left reasonably clean by the tenant having regard to the condition of the premises at the start of the tenancy`
        OR  (
                c's `the amount is the cost of replacing locks or other security devices altered, removed or added by the tenant without the consent of the lessor`
            AND NOT c's `section 50ZD(2) applies`
            )
        OR  c's `the amount is an amount the tenant is liable to pay to the lessor for a breach of the agreement`
        OR  (
                c's `the security bond includes the prescribed pet bond amount`
            AND (
                    c's `the amount is the reasonable cost of repairs or restoration as a result of damage caused by a pet kept at the premises`
                OR  c's `the amount is the reasonable cost of fumigating the premises because a pet kept on the premises is capable of carrying parasites that can affect humans`
                OR  c's `the amount is other reasonable costs arising out of the keeping of the pet on the premises`
                )
            )
        )

§§§ `81F. Notice of security bond release application to other parties`

DECLARE `bond release notice facts` HAS
    `the application is made by each person known to the bond administrator as a party to the agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the bond administrator has given written notice of the application to each known party who did not make the application` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) s.81F
@export Decide whether the bond administrator must give notice of a security bond release application to other known parties
GIVEN f IS A `bond release notice facts` @desc TRUE when the application is not made by each person known to the bond administrator as a party. The bond administrator must then give written notice to each known party who did not make the application.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the bond administrator must give written notice of the application to each known party who did not make the application` IF
    NOT f's `the application is made by each person known to the bond administrator as a party to the agreement`

§§§ `81G. Agreeing to security bond release application`

DECLARE `bond response` HAS
    `the party was given notice of the application under section 81F(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the party has given the bond administrator written notice in the prescribed way of agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the party has given the bond administrator written notice in the prescribed way of dispute` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the bond administrator has paid any of the security bond under Division 2` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the bond administrator has given notice of the application to 1 or more parties under section 81F(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `at least 1 of the parties does not respond during the notice period and all of the parties do not otherwise agree during that period` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the parties do not otherwise agree to the application during the notice period` IS A BOOLEAN
    `each known party has made the application, agreed under section 81G or otherwise, or withdrawn a notice of dispute under section 81J` IS A BOOLEAN
    `each known party agrees to a variation of the application` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) s.81G
@export Decide whether a notified party may agree to a security bond release application under s.81G
GIVEN r IS A `bond response` @desc A party given s.81F(2) notice may agree by written notice to the bond administrator in the prescribed way.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the party may agree to the security bond release application` IF
    r's `the party was given notice of the application under section 81F(2)`

@ref Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) s.81H
@export Decide whether a notified party may dispute a security bond release application under s.81H
GIVEN r IS A `bond response` @desc A party given s.81F(2) notice may dispute by written notice in the prescribed way. The bond administrator may accept a late dispute only if it has not paid any of the bond under Division 2.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the party may dispute the security bond release application` IF
        r's `the party was given notice of the application under section 81F(2)`
    AND (
            NOT r's `the bond administrator has paid any of the security bond under Division 2`
        OR  r's `the party has given the bond administrator written notice in the prescribed way of dispute`
        )

@ref Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) s.81I
@export Decide whether the bond administrator must refer the application to the Commissioner under s.81I
GIVEN r IS A `bond response` @desc Referral is required if s.81F(2) notice was given and there is a dispute, a non-response without all-party agreement, or the parties do not otherwise agree during the notice period.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the bond administrator must refer the application to the Commissioner` IF
        r's `the bond administrator has given notice of the application to 1 or more parties under section 81F(2)`
    AND (
            r's `the party has given the bond administrator written notice in the prescribed way of dispute`
        OR  r's `at least 1 of the parties does not respond during the notice period and all of the parties do not otherwise agree during that period`
        OR  r's `the parties do not otherwise agree to the application during the notice period`
        )

@ref Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) s.81K
@export Decide whether the bond administrator must pay the security bond as stated in the application under s.81K
GIVEN r IS A `bond response` @desc Payment is required if each known party has made the application, agreed under s.81G or otherwise, or withdrawn a dispute under s.81J, or if each known party agrees to a variation.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the bond administrator must pay the security bond as stated in the application` IF
        r's `each known party has made the application, agreed under section 81G or otherwise, or withdrawn a notice of dispute under section 81J`
    OR  r's `each known party agrees to a variation of the application`

§§ `Fixtures`

`pet bond after pet gone` MEANS `partial bond release application` WITH
    `the application is under section 81C` IS TRUE,
    `the application is for only part of a security bond to be released` IS TRUE,
    `that part is to be paid to the tenant or 1 or more of the cotenants` IS TRUE,
    `the rent payable under the residential tenancy agreement has been reduced` IS FALSE,
    `the tenant paid the prescribed pet bond amount and the pet is no longer being kept on the premises` IS TRUE,
    `other prescribed circumstances exist` IS FALSE

`unpaid rent claim` MEANS `bond claim` WITH
    `the amount is the reasonable cost of repairs to the premises, or restoration to original condition, as a result of damage other than fair wear and tear caused by the tenant, an occupant or an invitee of the tenant` IS FALSE,
    `the amount is the reasonable cost of repairs to or replacement of chattels provided with the premises as a result of damage other than fair wear and tear caused by the tenant, an occupant or an invitee of the tenant` IS FALSE,
    `the amount is rent or other charges owing and payable under the agreement or this Act` IS TRUE,
    `the amount is the cost of cleaning any part of the premises not left reasonably clean by the tenant having regard to the condition of the premises at the start of the tenancy` IS FALSE,
    `the amount is the cost of replacing locks or other security devices altered, removed or added by the tenant without the consent of the lessor` IS FALSE,
    `section 50ZD(2) applies` IS FALSE,
    `the amount is an amount the tenant is liable to pay to the lessor for a breach of the agreement` IS FALSE,
    `the amount is prescribed as an amount for which the lessor is not entitled to payment from the security bond` IS FALSE,
    `the security bond includes the prescribed pet bond amount` IS FALSE,
    `the amount is the reasonable cost of repairs or restoration as a result of damage caused by a pet kept at the premises` IS FALSE,
    `the amount is the reasonable cost of fumigating the premises because a pet kept on the premises is capable of carrying parasites that can affect humans` IS FALSE,
    `the amount is other reasonable costs arising out of the keeping of the pet on the premises` IS FALSE

`fair wear and tear only` MEANS `bond claim` WITH
    `the amount is the reasonable cost of repairs to the premises, or restoration to original condition, as a result of damage other than fair wear and tear caused by the tenant, an occupant or an invitee of the tenant` IS FALSE,
    `the amount is the reasonable cost of repairs to or replacement of chattels provided with the premises as a result of damage other than fair wear and tear caused by the tenant, an occupant or an invitee of the tenant` IS FALSE,
    `the amount is rent or other charges owing and payable under the agreement or this Act` IS FALSE,
    `the amount is the cost of cleaning any part of the premises not left reasonably clean by the tenant having regard to the condition of the premises at the start of the tenancy` IS FALSE,
    `the amount is the cost of replacing locks or other security devices altered, removed or added by the tenant without the consent of the lessor` IS FALSE,
    `section 50ZD(2) applies` IS FALSE,
    `the amount is an amount the tenant is liable to pay to the lessor for a breach of the agreement` IS FALSE,
    `the amount is prescribed as an amount for which the lessor is not entitled to payment from the security bond` IS FALSE,
    `the security bond includes the prescribed pet bond amount` IS FALSE,
    `the amount is the reasonable cost of repairs or restoration as a result of damage caused by a pet kept at the premises` IS FALSE,
    `the amount is the reasonable cost of fumigating the premises because a pet kept on the premises is capable of carrying parasites that can affect humans` IS FALSE,
    `the amount is other reasonable costs arising out of the keeping of the pet on the premises` IS FALSE

`one party applied` MEANS `bond release notice facts` WITH
    `the application is made by each person known to the bond administrator as a party to the agreement` IS FALSE,
    `the bond administrator has given written notice of the application to each known party who did not make the application` IS FALSE

#EVAL `a partial security bond release application may be made` `pet bond after pet gone`
#EVAL `the lessor is entitled to payment of the amount from the security bond` `unpaid rent claim`
#EVAL `the lessor is entitled to payment of the amount from the security bond` `fair wear and tear only`
#EVAL `the bond administrator must give written notice of the application to each known party who did not make the application` `one party applied`
#ASSERT `a partial security bond release application may be made` `pet bond after pet gone` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the lessor is entitled to payment of the amount from the security bond` `unpaid rent claim` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the lessor is entitled to payment of the amount from the security bond` `fair wear and tear only` EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `the bond administrator must give written notice of the application to each known party who did not make the application` `one party applied` EQUALS TRUE

`post termination release` MEANS `security bond release application` WITH
    `the applicant is one, some or all of the parties to the residential tenancy agreement` IS TRUE,
    `the application is in the approved form` IS TRUE,
    `the application states the amount of the security bond to be paid to each party` IS TRUE,
    `the residential tenancy agreement has terminated` IS TRUE,
    `the tenant or all cotenants have delivered up vacant possession of the premises` IS FALSE,
    `the parties to the agreement have agreed in writing to terminate the agreement` IS FALSE,
    `section 81D applies` IS FALSE

`all known parties agreed` MEANS `bond response` WITH
    `the party was given notice of the application under section 81F(2)` IS TRUE,
    `the party has given the bond administrator written notice in the prescribed way of agreement` IS TRUE,
    `the party has given the bond administrator written notice in the prescribed way of dispute` IS FALSE,
    `the bond administrator has paid any of the security bond under Division 2` IS FALSE,
    `the bond administrator has given notice of the application to 1 or more parties under section 81F(2)` IS TRUE,
    `at least 1 of the parties does not respond during the notice period and all of the parties do not otherwise agree during that period` IS FALSE,
    `the parties do not otherwise agree to the application during the notice period` IS FALSE,
    `each known party has made the application, agreed under section 81G or otherwise, or withdrawn a notice of dispute under section 81J` IS TRUE,
    `each known party agrees to a variation of the application` IS FALSE

#EVAL `a security bond release application may be made` `post termination release`
#EVAL `the bond administrator must pay the security bond as stated in the application` `all known parties agreed`
#ASSERT `a security bond release application may be made` `post termination release` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the bond administrator must pay the security bond as stated in the application` `all known parties agreed` EQUALS TRUE
